  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole adult reconstruction retaining pear-shaped torso, long neck and large grasping thumb; not a juvenile or skeletal display.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original living reconstruction. Seven metres is a taxon-level NHM estimate, not the measured total length of GPIT/RE/7288. Fossil mounts include reconstructed elements and poses; soft tissues and colour remain interpretative. Fabian is juvenile and used only as an auxiliary anatomical reference, not adult proportions.\",\"zh\":\"完整成体活体复原。7米为NHM属级估值，非GPIT/RE/7288实测全长。骨架装架含补配与姿态复原，软组织颜色不确定。Fabian是幼体，仅辅助解剖，不作为成体比例。\"},\"inventory_ordinal\":343,\"name\":{\"en\":\"Plateosaurus\",\"zh\":\"板龙\"},\"taxon\":\"Plateosaurus trossingensis (older anatomical source uses P. engelhardti)\",\"classification\":\"Dinosauria, Saurischia, Sauropodomorpha, Plateosauridae\",\"scale\":{\"total_length_m\":7.0,\"basis\":\"NHM taxon estimate; adult range independently described as 5-10 m by University of Bonn.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Pear-shaped trunk with deeper broad pelvis/abdomen and narrowing chest, not uniform sauropod barrel.\",\"Long gently curved neck with small elongate head, long tapering counterbalance tail.\",\"Two robust weight-bearing hindlimbs; shorter arms held free with inward-facing palms, never flat weight-bearing pronated hands.\",\"Five manual digits with clearly enlarged curved digit-I thumb claw; reduced outer digits, not five identical spikes.\",\"Complete animal with readable negative spaces around elbows, neck and tail; original shape combination must survive comparison with Massospondylus and Mussaurus.\"],\"specimen_basis\":\"Adult mounted GPIT/RE/7288 on right in Mallison2014 photo; published digital study supplements skull and hand with other named specimens, not claimed single untouched skeleton. Fabian juvenile auxiliary photo is visibly separate.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole adult reconstruction retaining pear-shaped torso, long neck and large grasping thumb; not a juvenile or skeletal display.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original living reconstruction. Seven metres is a taxon-level NHM estimate, not the measured total length of GPIT/RE/7288. Fossil mounts include reconstructed elements and poses; soft tissues and colour remain interpretative. Fabian is juvenile and used only as an auxiliary anatomical reference, not adult proportions.\",\"zh\":\"完整成体活体复原。7米为NHM属级估值，非GPIT/RE/7288实测全长。骨架装架含补配与姿态复原，软组织颜色不确定。Fabian是幼体，仅辅助解剖，不作为成体比例。\"},\"inventory_ordinal\":343,\"name\":{\"en\":\"Plateosaurus\",\"zh\":\"板龙\"},\"taxon\":\"Plateosaurus trossingensis (older anatomical source uses P. engelhardti)\",\"classification\":\"Dinosauria, Saurischia, Sauropodomorpha, Plateosauridae\",\"scale\":{\"total_length_m\":7.0,\"basis\":\"NHM taxon estimate; adult range independently described as 5-10 m by University of Bonn.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Pear-shaped trunk with deeper broad pelvis/abdomen and narrowing chest, not uniform sauropod barrel.\",\"Long gently curved neck with small elongate head, long tapering counterbalance tail.\",\"Two robust weight-bearing hindlimbs; shorter arms held free with inward-facing palms, never flat weight-bearing pronated hands.\",\"Five manual digits with clearly enlarged curved digit-I thumb claw; reduced outer digits, not five identical spikes.\",\"Complete animal with readable negative spaces around elbows, neck and tail; original shape combination must survive comparison with Massospondylus and Mussaurus.\"],\"specimen_basis\":\"Adult mounted GPIT/RE/7288 on right in Mallison2014 photo; published digital study supplements skull and hand with other named specimens, not claimed single untouched skeleton. Fabian juvenile auxiliary photo is visibly separate.\"}"
  },
